{"title":"Rolle's Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Rolle's theorem</b> is an important theorem among the class of results regarding the value of the derivative on an interval.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rolle%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c320754a36aaec178e61f04bfcbac41c0bf675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be continous on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and differentiable on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecf8666cca5f1d089b9c656be83f9e09d0abd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists$\" width=\"9\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb0282d88093562b34ff10aea38d63cecfd5d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in (a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b2f2b54deaf59958f8b5a13885f10b5c93c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(c)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rolle%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The result is trivial for the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc660c1a05ec6f54a3a2f57a03a47e3eaa23649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f([a,b])=\\{f(a)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" />. Hence, let us assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a non-constant function. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbce4c453e5dbd5353e06c8c6e58b2e0d592bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\sup\\{f([a,b])\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bcecd82871ae4cb9ccf9b2da9d2ec1bbf513980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\inf\\{f([a,b])\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" />\nWithout loss of generality, we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befaacaa68213f4070c07312f5b68558d1d9fa0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\neq f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum-minimum_theorem\" title=\"Maximum-minimum theorem\">Maximum-minimum theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e3aacb7d0e89a945a674404eca3be8d0c282a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists c\\in (a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b896af78e6e980462de15c0906b361b5c9fcc756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(c)=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Assume if possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e31a23e57225298de2f817603a0a97f9a00981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(c)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e36d2473b947fc01d1e098736c6570d7313cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon=\\frac{f&#39;(c)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b83e87155f6b030dd1fc6df10d0d20a85705e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists \\delta&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88fa4e31baa2b4446897e96614fdc4649a2ac8cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in V_{\\delta}(c)\\implies |\\frac{f(x)-f(c)}{x-c}-f&#39;(c)|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"317\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c0544c8ba7007c951d806aebfe33164291a05ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall x\\in V_{\\delta}(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3914adebe7d8e2ee36b32eb7ff57677c8e6441f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(x)-f(c)}{x-c}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/0164f8dd12daa9631d114f28ba3dddfaea2e14e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&gt;f(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043b159e143ce3b94d8770e35ad86bcdcaa96465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (c,c+\\delta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />, contradicting the assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55646bbf92355779b357feafd057262ae76d25d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is a maximum.\n</p><p>Similarly we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a768183240a550f75d0ad657b29851ffd0a70e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(c)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> leads to contradiction.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b2f2b54deaf59958f8b5a13885f10b5c93c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(c)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<p align=\"RIGHT\">QED</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rolle%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lagrange%27s_mean_value_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lagrange&#39;s mean value theorem\">Lagrange's mean value theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">Calculus</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 141/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4813/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6418:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234902 and revision id 106019. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}